From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:50:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Diagnostic: the Atlantic face jet against the inflow nudging
 and the radiation direction (not for the merge)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The face (25, 1, 4), a partial bottom cell on the Atlantic open side, holds v = −0.90 m/s while GLORYS gives
−0.26 there and the first interior face +0.28. ObliqueRadiation decides inflow versus outflow of a NormalFlow
condition from the first interior face, so this face counts as inflow: no radiation, 1-day nudging only.
config_smoke_test_inflow_1h.toml nudges over 1 hour instead; config_smoke_test_face_direction.toml decides the
direction on the boundary face (radiation_face_direction.jl, [boundaries] classify_by_boundary_velocity = true).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Abhhvkp8Pai9cvvctGUDX5
